.TH GIT-SYNC 1 "2026-11-23" "git-sync" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
git-sync \- update all local branches from their remotes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git-sync
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git-sync
fetches from the remote whose
.I <remote>/HEAD
ref exists (usually
.BR origin ),
then fast-forwards every local branch that is behind its upstream. A branch not
tracking that remote is compared with the same-named branch on it.
.PP
Remote-tracking refs that no longer exist on the remote are pruned. Tags are
neither fetched nor pruned. Without a
.I <remote>/HEAD
ref it fails with
.BR "could not find a remote" ;
create one with
.BR "git remote set-head origin \-a" .
.PP
Requires git 2.36 or newer.
.SH BRANCHES
Each local branch is handled on its own. Warnings are not failures.
.TP
.B Behind its upstream
Fast-forwarded, including the checked-out branch.
.TP
.B Unpushed or diverged
Left alone with a warning. A diverged branch stays stale until it is rebased or
merged by hand.
.TP
.B Upstream deleted
Kept with a warning, unless
.B \-\-prune
is given.
.TP
.B Identical, or no matching remote branch
Untouched.
.SH WORKTREES
A branch checked out in another worktree is fast-forwarded there. It is left
alone with a warning if that
worktree has changes to tracked files, or a rebase, bisect, merge, cherry-pick
or revert in progress, or if the fast-forward itself fails. Untracked files are
ignored.
.PP
A branch checked out in several worktrees is always left alone with a warning.
.SH OUTPUT
One line per change, giving the commit the branch was at before. Output always
includes ANSI colour codes, and warnings are written to standard output.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-prune
Delete branches whose upstream is gone, but only if their changes are already
in the default branch, whether merged, rebased, or squashed. Requires git 2.40
or newer. Anything that cannot be proven merged is kept with a warning.
.IP
Deletion is forced, with no prompt and no dry run. Restore a branch with
.B git branch
.I name sha
using the
.B was
commit from the output. If the checked-out branch is deleted, the default
branch is checked out first. A branch checked out in another worktree is kept,
and so is the checked-out branch when the default branch is checked out in
another worktree.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage information and exit. Git intercepts
.B git sync \-\-help
to show this page, so use
.B \-h
for the usage text.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-
End of options. Any other argument is an error.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Exits 0 on success, including with warnings. Any error exits 1 and prints a line
beginning
.B error:
to standard error. The first error for a branch stops the run, so branches after
it, in ASCII order, are not synced.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
$ git sync
Updated branch main (was 8915328).
warning: 'feature\-123' was deleted on origin
$ git sync \-\-prune
Deleted branch feature\-123 (was 7c24329).
$ git \-C ~/src/my\-repo sync
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR git\-fetch (1),
.BR git\-worktree (1)
